'' RUN: a span where an 'x() as T' parameter is wanted (docs/tiko-slices RFC-0003 §6): the callee
'' sees a 0-based array over the span's elements -- lbound/ubound, reads, writes landing in the
'' source, an empty span (0 to -1), string elements; a 'byval span' overload beats an array one,
'' and 'f()' still picks the array one; ERASE in the callee clears the source's elements in place.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: -target windows-x86_64 -w all tests/codegen/src/array-slice-desc.tiko -o tests/codegen/arrayslicedesc.exe
'' ENV: TIKO_LIBPATH=build/obj/rtlib/windows-x86_64
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-NOT: warning
'' EXPECT-FILE: tests/codegen/arrayslicedesc.exe
'' RUN: tests/codegen/arrayslicedesc.exe
'' EXPECT-RUN-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: total 9 11
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: bumped 1 102 104 5
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: bounds 0 2
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: bounds 0-1
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: span
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: array
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: cleared 104 0 0
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: cd
